        "severity": "minor",
        "file": "agent-orchestration/topology/lib/lead.mjs",
        "line": 40009,
        "claim": "With the default ack timeout shorter than the 60 s poll interval, a fresh probe that times out reads `unproven`, never `unresponsive`, which delays detecting a hung lead by at least one poll interval.",
        "evidence": "probeMiss treats any probe pending less than LEAD_POLL_INTERVAL_MS as undelivered.",
        "fix": "In a follow-up, document the detection delay in the CHANGELOG, or have recovery wait at least one poll interval before judging."
      },
      {
        "severity": "note",
        "file": "agent-orchestration/topology/lib/lead-recovery.mjs",
        "line": 1846,
        "claim": "I reviewed revision 0f1c6e2c (patch sha256 fb195d21…), the same patch as requests d69d3462 and 281e43cc, which were blocked for scope and then for evidence. All files are now within the touches, and all required checks pass as host-run results with output (agent-orchestration unit 1348 and 0, task-management unit 1726 and 0, plugin-rsync tests with 0 failing). Criterion 1: the cached-proof check is repeated under the probe lock, so no probe is minted or rung while a proof within its TTL exists, and every probe and ring outcome records requested_by and reason. Criterion 2: lead status reports the current reason (last_error is blanked when the lead is responsive now, neutral recovery carries the current error) and a resolved checkout-repair alert is cleared and journaled. Criterion 3: `withdraw --id` (and positional or --message for wait, reply and dispose) works, and dispose accepts already delivered standing mail for its recipient, so a duplicate delivery is a deduplicated no-op."
      }
    ],
